      "reviewed_current_text": "This paper proposes a conditional interoperable certificate-methods architecture, not an executed primitive-owner census or a passage-verified conclusion from the frozen corpus. Two surface-specific exact proof producers may use different internal representations and theorem routes. Their outputs can be compared only through one common semantic schema that distinguishes conjugacy, roots and primitivity, external inversion, self-reciprocity, repetitions, cutoff evidence, termination, completeness, and positive or negative replay payloads. One independent validator must check that schema and dispatch producer-specific proof types without trusting producer status.",
